Z||000003||tomanyfieros||12-30-2001||11:09 AM||||i have the 95 TA seats in my 87 GT, there is one problem though... (but im lucky, so i didnot have this problem)<BR>the seats in a 95 TA, (the ones i have) are fully loaded seats, lumbar, black leather, ect. the SEAT COVER is like 1500! my dad sold a pair to a DEALER for 2500 for both, one seat was pretty messed up! and the dealer bought them! i feel special... i got mine for free!!! i luv my dad!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||12-30-2001||11:35 AM||||My personal experience with both normal and power F-body seats has been this:<BR>You can get the passenger seat to sit just like the Fiero seat because the Fiero seat tracks will bolt on it.<BR>The driver's seat is a different story. The seats that I have used (a set from a plain Camaro-cloth/non-powered and a leather lumbar set from a Trans-Am) have a tilt feature to raise the front of the seat slightly. Because of this, the bolt pattern on the bottom of the seat does not match that of the Fiero tracks, so you have to use the F-body tracks. These raise the seat up higher than stock. If you are tall, you might not like it. I am 5'8" and my hair touches the drooping headliner.<BR>If you were inclined to redrill the mounting holes in the bottom of the F-body seat, then you could probably use the Fiero tracks and have the stock height. But if you have the power lumbar seats, then the pump will have to be relocated from the bottom of the seat.||||reg||1
